{
  "title": "DISH (Diffuse Idiopathic Skeletal Hyperostosis)",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/spine/2045/dish-diffuse-idiopathic-skeletal-hyperostosis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 15 2026",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "SUMMARY",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis (DISH), also known as Forestier disease, is a common disorder of unknown etiology characterized by enthesopathy of the spine and extremities. It usually presents with back pain and spinal stiffness",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be confirmed with radiographs of the spine. A CT scan should be performed whenever there is concern for a fracture following low-energy trauma",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually activity modification, physical therapy, and bisphosphonate therapy. Associated spinal fractures are treated with long-segment spinal fusion",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "overall incidence is 6-12%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "uncommon in patients <50 y/o",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "prevalence",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": ">50 y/o (25% males, 15% females)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": ">80 y/o (28% males, 26% females)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "less common in Black, Native-American, and Asian populations",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs anywhere in the spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most common in the **thoracic spine (right side) > cervical spine > lumbar spine**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**postulated to be due to the protective effect of the pulsatile aorta on the left side of the thoracic spine**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/dish.jpg",
                          "caption": "CT T spine DISH"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**symmetric** in the cervical and lumbar spine (syndesmophytes on both the left and right sides of the spine)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**gout**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**hyperlipidemia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**diabetes**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ETIOLOGY",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lumbar spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**lumbar spinal stenosis**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cervical spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dysphagia and stridor",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/cervical%20dish.jpg",
                      "caption": "CT cervical spine DISH"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "hoarseness",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "sleep apnea",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "difficulty with intubation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**cervical myelopathy**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "spine fracture and instability",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ankylosis of the vertebral segments proximal and distal to the fracture creates long lever arms that may cause displacement, even after low-energy injuries",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**hyperextension** injuries are common",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "seemingly minor, low-energy injury mechanisms may result in unstable fracture patterns",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "have increased vigilance in patients with pain and an ankylosed spine",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**often asymptomatic and discovered incidentally**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "thoracic and lumbar involvement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**mild chronic back pain**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**usually minimal because of stabilization of spinal segments through ankylosis**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**stiffness**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**worse in the morning**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "**aggravated by cold weather**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "cervical involvement (with large anterior osteophytes)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pain and stiffness",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**dysphagia**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/cervical%20dish.jpg",
                      "caption": "CT cervical spine DISH"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**stridor**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**hoarseness**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**sleep apnea**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "decreased ROM of the spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "neurologic symptoms of myelopathy or spinal stenosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "AP and lateral of the involved spinal region",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**non-marginal syndesmophytes at 3 successive levels (4 contiguous vertebrae)**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/xray-lumbar-ap-nonmarginal.jpg",
                      "caption": "Shows nonmarginal syndesmophytes"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thoracic spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "radiographic findings typically appear on the right side",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/thoracic%20ap.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        },
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/thoracic%20lateral.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "thoracic spine is often involved in isolation",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "particularly from T7-11",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "1",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "radiographic examination of this area is helpful when attempting to establish a diagnosis of DISH",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/right%20side%20thoracic..jpg",
                              "caption": "Shows right sided DISH involvement"
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "4",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "cervical spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anterior bone formation with **preservation of the disc space** (best seen on a lateral cervical view)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/question/894/images/xray-cervical-lateral-shows%20dish-google.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lateral cervical radiographs are useful for differentiating DISH from AS",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "AS will demonstrate disc space ossification (fusion between vertebral bodies)",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [
                            {
                              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/question/90/images/xray-cervical-lat-shows%20as.jpg",
                              "caption": ""
                            }
                          ],
                          "importance": "1",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "lumbar spine",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/lumbar%20ap.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    },
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/lumbar%20lateral.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symmetrical syndesmophytes (on both the left and right side of the lumbar spine)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "involvement of other joints (e.g. the elbow)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/elbow.jpg",
                      "caption": ""
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Technetium bone scan",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "increased **uptake** in areas of involvement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "may mimic metastatic disease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT or MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "patients with DISH, neck pain, and a history of trauma must be evaluated for occult fracture with CT",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "",
          "table": [
            {
              "header": true,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 3,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "DISH vs. Ankylosing Spondylitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "*DISH*",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "<i>Ankylosing Spondylitis</i>",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Syndesmophytes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Nonmarginal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/syndesmophyte%20illustration.jpg",
                          "caption": "Shows difference between marginal and nonmarginal syndesmophytes"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Marginal",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Radiographs",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "\"Flowing candle wax\"",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/xray-cervical-lateral-shows%20dish-google_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "\"Bamboo spine\"",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/romanus.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Squaring of vertebral bodies",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/romanus.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "\"Shiny corners\" at the attachment of the annulus fibrosus (Romanus lesions)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/romanus.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Disc space",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Preservation of the disc space",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "AS in the cervical spine may show ossification of the disc space",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2045/images/xray-cervical-lat-shows%20as_moved.jpg",
                          "caption": ""
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Osteopenia",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "No osteopenia (rather, there may be increased radiodensity)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Osteopenia present",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "HLA",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "No evidence of an association with HLA-B27",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Associated with HLA-B8 (common in patients who have both DISH and diabetes)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Strong association with HLA-B27",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Age group",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Older patients (middle-aged)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "Younger patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "header": false,
              "cells": [
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "SI joint involvement",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "colspan": 0,
                  "bullets": [
                    {
                      "text": "No involvement (SI joint abnormality generally excludes a diagnosis of DISH)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
